`test-sink` pushes one synthetic notification through one configured sink.
A name that is not in the config is refused (2) before anything is built;
a delivery that fails is a 1, the act's own code.

```console
$ zenwatch test-sink --config tests/cmd/fixtures/valid.json5 pager
? 2
Error: sink "pager" is not in tests/cmd/fixtures/valid.json5 (which has: hook, mail, ops, page)

```

The exec sink, against a program that is not there: the probe says so, and
the delivery fails.

```console
$ zenwatch test-sink --config tests/cmd/fixtures/valid.json5 page
? 1
test-sink page: probe — probe: /usr/local/bin/page-oncall not found
Error: test-sink page: delivery via exec failed

Caused by:
    transport: spawn /usr/local/bin/page-oncall: No such file or directory (os error 2)

```
